 quality, explainability, robustness, and reliability. ·         Collaborate closely with biologists, clinicians, bioinformaticians, and data engineers. ·         Contribute to scientific publications and future research projects in AI and precision oncology. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Candidate Profile Education ·         PhD (or equivalent experience) in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a related field. Technical Skills ·         Excellent Python programming skills. ·         Strong experience with generative AI and large language models. ·         Experience with agentic AI systems or complex orchestration architectures. ·         Good knowledge of information retrieval methods, RAG systems, vector databases, and/or knowledge graphs. ·         Familiarity with Linux environments and modern software development practices. Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience with LangGraph/LangChain, CrewAI, MCP, or similar frameworks. ·         Experience in biology, genomics, digital health, biomedical research, or oncology. ·         Scientific publications in AI, machine learning, bioinformatics, or computational biology. Personal Skills ·         Scientific curiosity. ·         Innovative mindset. ·         Ability to work autonomously. ·         Interest in interdisciplinary research. ·         Ability to transform exploratory ideas into robust and reusable solutions. Why Join Us ? AGORA offers a unique opportunity to help shape the next generation of AI systems for oncology by working on real-world scientific and clinical challenges alongside leading researchers and physicians. The project brings together several of the most exciting areas of modern artificial intelligence, including large language models (LLMs), multi-agent systems, knowledge graphs, multi-omics data integration, biological modelling, and clinical decision support. Beyond technology development, the ambition is to explore how agentic AI can become a genuine scientific partner—capable of reasoning over complex biomedical data, integrating up-to-date medical knowledge, supporting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. At the intersection of fundamental research, data science, systems biology, and precision medicine, Institut Curie provides a world-class research environment with access to unique clinical and molecular datasets. You will work within a highly interdisciplinary team and benefit from significant scientific freedom, opportunities for high-impact publications, international collaborations, and participation in the development of future national and European research initiatives. Contract Information Contract type: Fixed-term contract (CDD) Starting date: As soon as possible Duration: 18 months Salary: According to experience and institutional salary scales Benefits: Subsidized staff restaurant, public transportation reimbursement (70%), Private health insurance, Hybrid work opportunities Location: Institut Curie, Paris, France Application Send CV, cover letter, referees Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact fxwmd4gdzk5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 18 mois Quotité de travail Référence fxwmd4gdzk Publié le 26/08/2026 Postuler Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Research Engineer (M/F) (F/H) Localis