      "title": "Post-doctoral fellow in immunology (F/M)",
      "description": "Post-doctoral fellow in immunology (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Post-doctoral fellow in immunology (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/12/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Institut Curie Research Center Institut Curie is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a Hospital Group and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory Dr Eliane Piaggio's research group (Inserm U932, Paris, France, https://institut-curie.org/team/piaggio ) is part of an immunology department of 130 people headed by Dr Ana-Maria Lennon. The laboratory is located on the Institut Curie campus in central Paris.  The building is equipped with state-of-the-art facilities (imaging, proteomics, animal facilities, genomic and cytometric platforms). The Institute is home to some 1,500 scientists, including many foreign students and post-docs. The team comprises 13 members, including two bioinformaticians and a project manager. Missions The post-doctoral fellow's mission will be to achieve a project in translational immunology research related to the involvement of T regulatory lymphocytes in cancer. The candidate will be responsible for the development, handling and analysis of experiments, and for monitoring the bibliography. Projects will be developed under the supervision of Dr Eliane Piaggio.f cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required - PhD in immunology - Scientific publications attesting to successful completion of previous projects. - Required expertise in the Treg field. - Knowledge and former experience in cancer immunology would be an asset. Skills required - Expert in multiparametric FACS. - Experience in bioinformatics (RNASeq bulk or single cell analysis) would be an asset - Strong motivation, autonomy and excellent ability to work as part of a team. - A high level of integrity, accuracy and rigor are essential. - Proficiency in English is mandatory. All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term object-derived contract (COD) Starting date: December 1st 2026 Duration : 3 years Working time : full time Remuneration : according to the current Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV and letter of motivation Publication date: 27/07/2026 Deadline for application: November 30th 2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 26m6imih2d5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération De 36219.16 à 39808.96 € (Euros) par an Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 3 an(s) Quotité de travail Référence 26m6imih2d Publié le 27/07/2026 Postuler Post-doctoral fellow in immunology (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/12/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Institut Curie Research Center Institut Curie is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a Hospital Group and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory Dr Eliane Piaggio's research group (Inserm U932, Paris, France, https://institut-curie.org/team/piaggio ) is part of an immunology department of 130 people headed by Dr Ana-Maria Lennon. The laboratory is located on the Institut Curie campus in central Paris.  The building is equipped with state-of-the-art facilities (imaging, proteomics, animal facilities, genomic and cytometric platforms). The Institute is home to some 1,500 scientists, including many foreign students and post-docs. The team comprises 13 members, including two bioinformaticians and a project manager. Missions The post-doctoral fellow's mission will be to achieve a project in translational immunology research related to the involvement of T regulatory lymphocytes in cancer. The candidate will be responsible for the development, handling and analysis of experiments, and for monitoring the bibliography. Projects will be developed under the supervision of Dr Eliane Piaggio.f cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required - PhD in immunology - Scientific publications attesting to successful completion of previous projects. - Required expertise in the Treg field. - Knowledge and former experience in cancer immunology would be an asset. Skills required - Expert in multiparametric FACS. - Experience in bioinformatics (RNASeq bulk or single cell analysis) would be an asset - Strong motivation, autonomy and excellent ability to work as part of a team. - A high level of integrity, accuracy and rigor are essential. - Proficiency in English is mandatory. All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term object-derived contract (COD) Starting date: December 1st 2026 Duration : 3 years Working time : full time Remuneration : according to the current Benefits: Collective ca