    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/0eo2dopdcu": {
      "title": "Paramètres d’accessibilité",
      "description": "Project Engineer in Synthetic Chemistry (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Project Engineer in Synthetic Chemistry (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/09/2026 Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The 'Chemistry and Modelling for Cancer Biology' unit (UMR9187) is located at the Institut Curie research centre in Orsay. It is an interdisciplinary unit dedicated to designing and synthesising molecular probes and anti-cancer drug candidates and studying their mechanisms of action. The unit comprises 50 people and is supported by: - three research teams. - Two cross-disciplinary divisions (modelling and biology). - the ‘Chimiothèque' platform, which is one of the largest in France with almost 13,000 compounds resulting from 70 years of research. https://institut-curie.org/unit/umr9187-u1196 https://institut-curie.org/team/verga Missions Description of the activities Synthesizing heteroaromatic compounds: -        Implement and carry out one or more synthetic methods relevant to a specific field of chemistry. -        Select appropriate synthetic techniques and develop procedures and protocols. -        Monitor the progress and results of syntheses performed. -        Conduct literature reviews on specific issues to update your knowledge. -        Develop experimental procedures and prepare reports on the results of syntheses and their interpretation. -        Monitor scientific and technological developments. -        Provide guidance on selecting and implementing synthesis methods appropriate for solving the problem at hand. -        Share knowledge and skills with doctoral and postdoctoral students. -        Supervise and lead a team. -        Receive training and stay informed about chemical hazards. -        Apply and enforce health and safety rules, including any updates. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Master's degree in Chemistry -        Desired professional experience: One to two years' experience in a synthetic chemistry laboratory. Knowledge -        Chemistry (in-depth knowledge) -        Techniques for developing a family of molecules (in-depth knowledge). -        Methods for purifying and identifying molecules or chemical species (general knowledge). -        Appropriate physicochemical analytical methods (separation techniques, structural determination techniques, analysis, etc.). -        Synthesized molecules (basic concepts) -        Occupational hazards -        Professional environment and networks -        Organization and operation of higher education and public research -        Intellectual Property Law Desired operational skills -        Apply at least one chemical synthesis technique with proficiency. -        Use software to interpret results. -        Use software to draw chemical compounds. -        Follow health and safety guidelines. Skills required -        English proficiency: B1 to B2 -        Computer skills: Microsoft Office/ChemDraw -        Required skills: independence, project management, leadership, teamwork, etc.IT skills -        Ability to work independently, managerial abilities, Aptitude for working in a team, collaboratively. -        Ability to communicate All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : One-year fixed-term contract that may lead to a permanent contract Starting date: 01/09/2026 Duration : 1 year Working time : full time - 39 hours per week Remuneration : according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Orsay Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references Publication date: 21/07/2026 Deadline for application: 01/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 0eo2dopdcu5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 1 an(s) Quotité de travail Référence 0eo2dopdcu Publié le 21/07/2026 Postuler Project Engineer in Synthetic Chemistry (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/09/2026 Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The 'Chemistry and Modelling for Cancer Biology' unit (UMR9187) is located at the Institut Curie research centre in Orsay. It is an interdisciplinary unit dedicated to designing and synthesising molecular probes and anti-cancer drug candidates and studying their mechanisms of action. The unit comprises 50 people and is supported by: - three research teams. - Two cross-disciplinary divisions (modelling and biology). - the ‘Chimiothèque' platform, which is one of the largest in France with almost 13,000 compounds resulting from 70 years of research. https://institut-curie.org/unit/umr9187-u1196 https://institut-curie.org/team/verga Missions Description of the activities Synthesizing heteroaromatic compounds: -        Implement and carry out one or more synthetic methods relevant to a specific field of chemistry. -        Select appropriate synthetic techniques and develop procedures and protocols. -        Monitor the progress and results of syntheses performed. -        Conduct literature reviews on specific issues to update your knowledge. -        Develop experimental procedures and prepare reports on the results of syntheses and their interpretation. -        Monitor scientific and technological developments. -        Provide guidance on selecting and implementing synthesis methods appropriate for solving the problem at hand. -        Share knowledge and skills with doctoral and postdoctoral students. -        Supervise and lead a team. -        Receive training and stay informed about chemical hazards. -        Apply and enforce health and safety rules, including any updates. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Master's degree in Chemistry -        Desired professional experience: One to two years' experience in a synthetic chemistry laboratory. Knowledge -        Chemistry (in-depth knowledge) -        Techniques for developing a family of molecules (in-depth knowledge). -        Methods for purifying and identifying molecules or chemical species (general knowledge). -        Appropriate physicochemical analytical methods (separation techniques, structural determination techniques, analysis, etc.). -        Synthesized molecules (basic concepts) -        Occupational hazards -        Professional environment and networks -        Organization and operation of higher education and public research -        Intellectual Property Law Desired operational skills -        Apply at least one chemical synthesis technique with proficiency. -        Use software to interpret results. -        Use software to draw chemical compounds. -        Follow health and safety guidelines. Skills required -        English proficiency: B1 to B2 -        Computer skills: Microsoft Office/ChemDraw -        Required skills: independence, project management, leadership, teamwork, etc.IT skills -        Ability to work independently, managerial abilities, Aptitude for working in a team, collaboratively. -        Ability to communicate All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : One-year fixed-term contract that may lead to a permanent contract Starting date: 01/09/2026 Duration : 1 year Working time : full time - 39 hours per week Remuneration : according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Orsay Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references Publication date: 21/07/2026 Deadline for application: 01/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 0eo2dopdcu5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste : CDD Durée du contrat : 1 an(s) Référence 0eo2dopdcu Publié le 21/07/2026 L'Université PSL (Paris Sciences & Lettres) Menu Footer RH CGU Crédits Politique de confidentialité Flux RSS de PSL Recrutement Gestion des cookies Vos paramètres de cookies Vous naviguez sur le site de l’Université PSL. L’Université PSL, responsable de traitement, utilise des cookies pour la réalisation de statistiques ainsi que pour l’optimisation du site. Vous pouvez accepter ou refuser l’utilisation de cookies, ainsi que personnaliser vos préférences. Nous conservons votre choix pendant 3 mois. Vous pouvez changer d’avis à tout moment en cliquant sur l’icône « Gestion des cookies » en bas à gauche sur toutes les pages de notre site internet. Plus d'informations Cookies obligatoire (session Drupal) Ces cookies sont strictement obligatoires au bon fonctionnent du site. Cookies vidéos Ils permettent la visualisation des vidéos sur notre site. (Youtube) Cookies de mesure d'audience Enregistrer mes choix Tout accepter Personnaliser"
    },
