    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/a4nlka4l2s": {
      "title": "Paramètres d’accessibilité",
      "description": "Study Engineer (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Study Engineer  (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/10/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center The Institut Curie is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory Institut Curie, CNRS UMR 144 – team Daniele Fachinetti: Molecular Mechanisms of Chromosome Dynamics Missions Our team Molecular Mechanisms of Chromosome Dynamics, led by Daniele Fachinetti, investigates the fundamental principles that ensure the faithful transmission of genetic material in mammalian cells. We combine cell biology, genetics, epigenetics, biochemistry, and imaging to understand how centromeres are established, maintained, and function throughout the cell cycle. We also study how their deregulation can lead to genome instability – a key driver of many pathologies, including cancer. Our team is seeking a motivated Study Engineer (IE) in Biology to contribute to a project investigating the role of aneuploidy, centromeres, and germline deletions in the transition from normal to tumoral states in neuroblastoma. The project focuses on human induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs), hiPSC-derived sympathoblasts, and neuroblastoma cell lines to better understand mechanisms of tumor initiation and progression. The successful candidate will be responsible for: - Maintenance and differentiation of hiPSCs and culture of several cell lines. - Lab management - Performing transfection experiments and molecular assays (including CRISPR technology) to modulate and analyze gene expression. - Conducting DNA, RNA, and protein extraction followed by downstream analyses (PCR, RT-qPCR, western blot). - Applying molecular biology techniques such as cloning and plasmid manipulation. - Collaborating closely with researchers to analyze experimental data and contribute to the advancement of the project Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Profile Education and competences -        Education: Master’s degree (MSc) in molecular and cellular biology, biotechnology, or a related field. -        Experience: At least 1-2 years of hands-on experience in mammalian cell culture and hiPSC/hESCs (mandatory). -        Solid background in cellular and molecular biology techniques (PCR, RT-qPCR, western blot, cloning, plasmids). Qualifications -        Good organizational skills, ability to work both independently and in a team. -        Rigor, motivation, and enthusiasm for research. -        Fluency in English All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : CDD Starting date: 01/10/2026 Duration : 12 months renewable Working time : full time Remuneration: from 29240.67 to 30396.75€/year according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation Publication date: 08/07/2026 Deadline for application: 30/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact a4nlka4l2s5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 12 mois Quotité de travail Référence a4nlka4l2s Publié le 08/07/2026 Postuler Study Engineer  (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/10/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center The Institut Curie is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory Institut Curie, CNRS UMR 144 – team Daniele Fachinetti: Molecular Mechanisms of Chromosome Dynamics Missions Our team Molecular Mechanisms of Chromosome Dynamics, led by Daniele Fachinetti, investigates the fundamental principles that ensure the faithful transmission of genetic material in mammalian cells. We combine cell biology, genetics, epigenetics, biochemistry, and imaging to understand how centromeres are established, maintained, and function throughout the cell cycle. We also study how their deregulation can lead to genome instability – a key driver of many pathologies, including cancer. Our team is seeking a motivated Study Engineer (IE) in Biology to contribute to a project investigating the role of aneuploidy, centromeres, and germline deletions in the transition from normal to tumoral states in neuroblastoma. The project focuses on human induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs), hiPSC-derived sympathoblasts, and neuroblastoma cell lines to better understand mechanisms of tumor initiation and progression. The successful candidate will be responsible for: - Maintenance and differentiation of hiPSCs and culture of several cell lines. - Lab management - Performing transfection experiments and molecular assays (including CRISPR technology) to modulate and analyze gene expression. - Conducting DNA, RNA, and protein extraction followed by downstream analyses (PCR, RT-qPCR, western blot). - Applying molecular biology techniques such as cloning and plasmid manipulation. - Collaborating closely with researchers to analyze experimental data and contribute to the advancement of the project Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Profile Education and competences -        Education: Master’s degree (MSc) in molecular and cellular biology, biotechnology, or a related field. -        Experience: At least 1-2 years of hands-on experience in mammalian cell culture and hiPSC/hESCs (mandatory). -        Solid background in cellular and molecular biology techniques (PCR, RT-qPCR, western blot, cloning, plasmids). Qualifications -        Good organizational skills, ability to work both independently and in a team. -        Rigor, motivation, and enthusiasm for research. -        Fluency in English All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : CDD Starting date: 01/10/2026 Duration : 12 months renewable Working time : full time Remuneration: from 29240.67 to 30396.75€/year according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation Publication date: 08/07/2026 Deadline for application: 30/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact a4nlka4l2s5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste : CDD Durée du contrat : 12 mois Référence a4nlka4l2s Publié le 08/07/2026 L'Université PSL (Paris Sciences & Lettres) Menu Footer RH CGU Crédits Politique de confidentialité Flux RSS de PSL Recrutement Gestion des cookies Vos paramètres de cookies Vous naviguez sur le site de l’Université PSL. L’Université PSL, responsable de traitement, utilise des cookies pour la réalisation de statistiques ainsi que pour l’optimisation du site. Vous pouvez accepter ou refuser l’utilisation de cookies, ainsi que personnaliser vos préférences. Nous conservons votre choix pendant 3 mois. Vous pouvez changer d’avis à tout moment en cliquant sur l’icône « Gestion des cookies » en bas à gauche sur toutes les pages de notre site internet. Plus d'informations Cookies obligatoire (session Drupal) Ces cookies sont strictement obligatoires au bon fonctionnent du site. Cookies vidéos Ils permettent la visualisation des vidéos sur notre site. (Youtube) Cookies de mesure d'audience Enregistrer mes choix Tout accepter Personnaliser"
