      "title": "Paramètres d’accessibilité",
      "description": "Laboratory Manager (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Laboratory Manager (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/10/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center The Institut Curie is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The Basto Lab ( https://curie.fr/equipe/basto ) investigates the fundamental mechanisms that ensure accurate cell division and tissue homeostasis, and how their disruption contributes to disease. Our research combines cell biology, genetics, developmental biology, advanced microscopy, and quantitative approaches to understand how centrosomes, the cytoskeleton, and cell division are regulated across different biological contexts. We use a multidisciplinary approach and a diverse range of experimental models, including cultured mammalian cells, Drosophila melanogaster , and mouse models, allowing us to address biological questions from molecules to whole organisms. The laboratory is part of Institut Curie, an internationally recognized research center at the forefront of cancer, cell, and developmental biology, offering access to outstanding core facilities. Missions We are seeking an experienced and highly organized Laboratory Manager to join our team. The successful candidate will play a central role in ensuring the smooth operation of the laboratory while actively contributing to ongoing research projects. This is an ideal position for someone who enjoys combining hands-on experimental work with laboratory management in a collaborative and dynamic research environment. We offer the opportunity to work in an internationally recognized research institute with access to state-of-the-art facilities and a stimulating scientific environment. The successful candidate will become an integral member of a collaborative team committed to addressing fundamental questions in cell and developmental biology. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus We are looking for a proactive and motivated scientist with excellent organizational skills and laboratory experience. -        Degree (BSc, MSc, or equivalent) in Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related discipline. -        Experience in an academic or biomedical research environment. -        Strong experience in mammalian cell culture and cell biology techniques. -        Excellent organizational and communication skills. -        Ability to work independently while supporting a multidisciplinary research team. -        Fluency in English (written and spoken) All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : Full-time permanent position (CDI) Starting date: October 2026 Working time : 39h Remuneration : Salary range from 28510.59€  to 29240.67€/year with potential adjustments based on the candidate's profile and internal compensation guidelines. Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 reference contacts Publication date: 06/07/2026 Deadline for application: 01/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+4, Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact pirkla6a8n5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDI Quotité de travail Référence pirkla6a8n Publié le 07/07/2026 Postuler Laboratory Manager (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  01/10/2026 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs