ernationally recognized research institute with access to state-of-the-art facilities and a stimulating scientific environment. The successful candidate will become an integral member of a collaborative team committed to addressing fundamental questions in cell and developmental biology. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus We are looking for a proactive and motivated scientist with excellent organizational skills and laboratory experience. -        Degree (BSc, MSc, or equivalent) in Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related discipline. -        Experience in an academic or biomedical research environment. -        Strong experience in mammalian cell culture and cell biology techniques. -        Excellent organizational and communication skills. -        Ability to work independently while supporting a multidisciplinary research team. -        Fluency in English (written and spoken) All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : Full-time permanent position (CDI) Starting date: October 2026 Working time : 39h Remuneration : Salary range from 28510.59€  to 29240.67€/year with potential adjustments based on the candidate's profile and internal compensation guidelines. Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 reference contacts Publication date: 06/07/2026 Deadline for application: 01/09/2026 Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+4, Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion